# firewall screen-ubuntu2604 -----------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Mock: The Firewall screen. web-01.example.net runs Ubuntu$
# 26.04 as shipped: ufw installed and inactive, ENABLED=no, no$
# rule, sshd socket-activated on [::]:22 (vmtest.md §4.9).$
$
# UFW Firewall Configuration ###################################$
$
  [ ] Firewall             Not Configured inactive$
$
# ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Installed            Yes$
  [ ] Status               Inactive$
  [+] Incoming policy      Deny$
  [ ] At boot              No$
$
# SSH ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  [::]:22              Not filtered$
   -  0.0.0.0:22           Not filtered$
$
# Rules --------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  No firewall rules configured$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Enable firewall      Let SSH through, deny the rest$
                           [ ] Lockout risk$
   2) Application Profiles Add, remove, apply$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-2 or q]:$
$
$

